Local ares patch: instruction-cache miss profiler (n64/profile/icsim/README in
BRINGUP_NOTES.md, "I-cache: trace-driven placement").

Apply with `git apply` in an ares checkout, then add one line to
Cartridge::ISViewer::messageChar (ares/n64/cartridge/isviewer.cpp), next to
the data-cache profiler's dcprof::message(c) if that patch is applied:

    icprof::message(c);

Runtime: ARES_ICPROF=<out.txt> enables it (the JIT emits its hooks only
then); ARES_ICPROF_PHASE=<physical address of g_n64_profile_phase>;
ARES_ICTRACE=<trace.bin> also records the code-line trace for icsim/trg.
The window is the host's DCPROF_START/DCPROF_STOP markers (N64_DCPROF=<frame>).

